        "original_id": "087cd1e8-4ecf-5d0d-aa57-2048dfd8e095",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: The Periodic Table of Videos, Hello Internet\n- People: Brady Haran, Sir Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, CGP Grey\n- Organizations: University of Nottingham, BBC News, YouTube\n- Topics: chemical elements, the periodic table\n\nFacts:\n- Brady John Haran was born on 18 June 1976.\n- Brady Haran is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist known for educational videos and documentary films for BBC News and for YouTube channels including Periodic Videos and Numberphile.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is published on YouTube and produced by Brady Haran.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos features Sir Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, and others at the University of Nottingham.\n- Hello Internet is an audio podcast hosted by CGP Grey and Brady Haran.",
